TETRAKLEIN LOCAL VALIDATION — CPU TIER SUMMARY
==============================================================================
Date:   2026-01-01 22:54 UTC
System: Linux-6.12.47+rpt-rpi-2712-aarch64-with-glibc2.36
Device: Raspberry Pi 5 (16 GB)
CPU:    ARM Cortex-A76 (4-Core)
Mode:   CPU-only execution (NumPy backend)

Scope of This Validation
------------------------
This report summarizes the results of a complete CPU-tier validation
chain executed on a Raspberry Pi 5. The objective was to evaluate
whether the TetraKlein execution model remains correct, deterministic,
and structurally sound under constrained, non-accelerated hardware.

This validation explicitly excludes GPU acceleration, real-time
throughput claims, and performance scaling analysis.


Validated Subsystems
--------------------
The following subsystems were validated at the CPU tier:

• Deterministic execution trace generation
• Algebraic Intermediate Representation (AIR) degree safety
• Contractive state evolution and stability bounds
• Hypercube spectral structure (analytic validation)
• Incremental Verifiable Computation (IVC) recursion structure
• Trace folding and subsampling correctness
• CPU-safe memory behavior under stress tests


Key Findings
------------
1. Determinism and Stability
   Execution traces are deterministic and reproducible across runs.
   State evolution remains contractive, with bounded residuals.

2. Cryptographic Structure
   AIR constraints respect degree limits suitable for STARK-style
   verification. No constraint growth or algebraic instability was
   observed.

3. IVC Structural Soundness
   Recursive folding preserves correctness and boundedness of state.
   Recursion depth logic remains valid independent of hardware speed.

4. Resource Discipline
   All validation steps complete within the memory and compute
   envelope of a Raspberry Pi 5, without reliance on acceleration.


What This Demonstrates
----------------------
• The TetraKlein execution model degrades gracefully without GPUs
• Core correctness does not depend on hardware acceleration
• Cryptographic structure is independent of throughput
• Determinism and safety properties hold on embedded-class hardware


What This Does NOT Claim
------------------------
This validation does not claim:

• Real-time performance on CPU-only hardware
• XR frame-rate feasibility
• Practical proof throughput without acceleration
• Production deployment readiness
• Hardware-independent performance characteristics

This report establishes correctness and feasibility, not speed.


Engineering Implications
------------------------
The results indicate that:

• Correctness and safety properties are hardware-agnostic
• Performance optimizations can be layered without altering logic
• GPU acceleration improves throughput, not correctness
• The system remains inspectable and auditable on simple hardware


Next Logical Steps
------------------
1. Cross-reference CPU-tier results with GPU-tier validation
2. Formalize hardware-tier separation in documentation
3. Expand CPU validation to additional edge cases
4. Use CPU tier as a regression and audit baseline


==============================================================================
FINAL STATEMENT
==============================================================================
This Raspberry Pi 5 validation demonstrates that the TetraKlein
execution model is structurally sound, deterministic, and
cryptographically well-formed under constrained hardware.

Performance acceleration enhances throughput but is not required
for correctness, stability, or verification logic.


